\li1 \v 2 \w Reaiah|strong="H7211"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Shobal|strong="H7732"\w* \w was the father of|strong="H3205"\w* \w Jahath|strong="H3189"\w*, \w and Jahath|strong="H3189"\w* \w was the father of|strong="H3205"\w* \w Ahumai|strong="H267"\w* \w and Lahad|strong="H3855"\w*. \w These|strong="H428"\w* \w were the clans|strong="H4940"\w* \w of the Zorathites|strong="H6882"\w*.
\b 
\li1 \v 3 \w These|strong="H428"\w* \w were the sons|strong="H1"\w*\f + \fr 4:3 \ft LXX (see also Vulgate); Hebrew \fqa These were of the father\f* \w of Etam|strong="H5862"\w*: \w Jezreel|strong="H3157"\w*, \w Ishma|strong="H3457"\w*, \w and Idbash|strong="H3031"\w*. \w And their sister|strong="H269"\w* \w was named|strong="H8034"\w* \w Hazzelelponi|strong="H6753"\w*. \v 4 \w Penuel|strong="H6439"\w* \w was the father|strong="H1"\w*\f + \fr 4:4 \ft Or \fqa the founder\ft ; also in verses 5, 12, 14, 17, 18, and possibly elsewhere\f* \w of Gedor|strong="H1446"\w*, \w and Ezer|strong="H5829"\w* \w was the father of|strong="H1"\w* \w Hushah|strong="H2364"\w*.
