\li1 \v 9 \w from the Hebronites|strong="H1121"\w*, \w Eliel|strong="H447"\w* \w the chief|strong="H8269"\w* \w and 80|strong="H8084"\w* \w of his relatives|strong="H251"\w*;
\li1 \v 10 \w and from the Uzzielites|strong="H1121"\w*, \w Amminadab|strong="H5992"\w* \w the chief|strong="H8269"\w* \w and 112|strong="H3967"\w* \w of his relatives|strong="H251"\w*.
\p \v 11 \w David|strong="H1732"\w* \w summoned|strong="H7121"\w* \w the priests|strong="H3548"\w* \w Zadok|strong="H6659"\w* \w and Abiathar|strong="H54"\w* \w and the Levites|strong="H3881"\w* \w Uriel|strong="H222"\w*, \w Asaiah|strong="H6222"\w*, \w Joel|strong="H3100"\w*, \w Shemaiah|strong="H8098"\w*, \w Eliel|strong="H447"\w*, \w and Amminadab|strong="H5992"\w*. \v 12 \w And he said|strong="H559"\w* to them, “\w You|strong="H859"\w* \w are the heads|strong="H7218"\w* \w of the Levitical|strong="H3881"\w* \w families|strong="H1"\w*. \w You|strong="H859"\w* \w and your relatives|strong="H251"\w* \w must consecrate yourselves|strong="H6942"\w* \w so that you may bring|strong="H5927"\w* \w the ark|strong="H727"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w the God|strong="H430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w to the place|strong="H413"\w* \w I have prepared|strong="H3559"\w* for it. \v 13 \w It was because|strong="H3588"\w* \w you Levites|strong="H859"\w* \w were not with us|strong="H3808"\w* \w the first time|strong="H4100"\w* \w that the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w our God|strong="H430"\w* \w burst forth in anger|strong="H6555"\w* against us. \w For|strong="H3588"\w* \w we did not|strong="H3808"\w* \w consult Him|strong="H1875"\w* \w about the proper order|strong="H4941"\w*.”
\s1 The Priests and Levites Carry the Ark
\p \v 14 \w So the priests|strong="H3548"\w* \w and Levites|strong="H3881"\w* \w consecrated themselves|strong="H6942"\w* \w to bring up|strong="H5927"\w* \w the ark|strong="H727"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w the God|strong="H430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*. \v 15 \w And the Levites|strong="H1121"\w* \w carried|strong="H5375"\w* \w the ark|strong="H727"\w* \w of God|strong="H430"\w* \w on their shoulders|strong="H3802"\w* \w with the poles|strong="H4133"\w*, \w as|strong="H834"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w had commanded|strong="H6680"\w* \w in accordance with the word|strong="H1697"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*.
\p \v 16 \w David also|strong="H1732"\w* \w told|strong="H559"\w* \w the leaders|strong="H8269"\w* \w of the Levites|strong="H3881"\w* \w to appoint|strong="H5975"\w* \w their relatives|strong="H251"\w* \w as singers|strong="H7891"\w* \w to lift up|strong="H7311"\w* \w their voices|strong="H6963"\w* \w with joy|strong="H8057"\w*, \w accompanied by musical|strong="H7892"\w* \w instruments|strong="H3627"\w*— \w harps|strong="H5035"\w*, \w lyres|strong="H3658"\w*, \w and cymbals|strong="H4700"\w*. \v 17 \w So the Levites|strong="H3881"\w* \w appointed|strong="H5975"\w* \w Heman|strong="H1968"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Joel|strong="H3100"\w*; \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w his brothers|strong="H251"\w*, \w Asaph|strong="H623"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Berechiah|strong="H1296"\w*; \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w their brothers|strong="H251"\w* \w the Merarites|strong="H1121"\w*, \w Ethan|strong="H387"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Kushaiah|strong="H6984"\w*; \v 18 \w and with them|strong="H5973"\w* \w their brothers|strong="H251"\w* \w next in rank|strong="H4932"\w*: \w Zechariah|strong="H2148"\w*,\f + \fr 15:18 \ft Several Hebrew manuscripts and most LXX manuscripts (see also verse 20 and \ref 1 Chronicles 16:5|1CH 16:5\ref*); most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa Zechariah son of \ft or \fqa Zechariah, Ben, \f* \w Jaaziel|strong="H3268"\w*, \w Shemiramoth|strong="H8070"\w*, \w Jehiel|strong="H3171"\w*, \w Unni|strong="H6042"\w*, \w Eliab|strong="H446"\w*, \w Benaiah|strong="H1141"\w*, \w Maaseiah|strong="H4641"\w*, \w Mattithiah|strong="H4993"\w*, \w Eliphelehu|strong="H466"\w*, \w Mikneiah|strong="H4737"\w*, \w and the gatekeepers|strong="H7778"\w* \w Obed-edom|strong="H5654"\w* \w and Jeiel|strong="H3273"\w*.\f + \fr 15:18 \ft Hebrew; some LXX manuscripts \fqa Obed-edom, Jeiel, and Azaziah \ft or \fqa Obed-edom, Jeiel, and Ozias\f*
\p \v 19 \w The musicians|strong="H7891"\w* \w Heman|strong="H1968"\w*, \w Asaph|strong="H623"\w*, \w and Ethan|strong="H387"\w* \w were to sound|strong="H8085"\w* \w the bronze|strong="H5178"\w* \w cymbals|strong="H4700"\w*. \v 20 \w Zechariah|strong="H2148"\w*, \w Aziel|strong="H5815"\w*,\f + \fr 15:20 \fqa Aziel \ft is a variant of \fqa Jaaziel\ft ; see verse 18.\f* \w Shemiramoth|strong="H8070"\w*, \w Jehiel|strong="H3171"\w*, \w Unni|strong="H6042"\w*, \w Eliab|strong="H446"\w*, \w Maaseiah|strong="H4641"\w*, \w and Benaiah|strong="H1141"\w* \w were to play the harps|strong="H5035"\w* \w according to|strong="H5921"\w* \w Alamoth|strong="H5961"\w*.\f + \fr 15:20 \fqa Alamoth\ft is probably a musical or liturgical term; here and in \ref Psalm 46:1|PSA 46:1\ref*.\f* \v 21 \w And Mattithiah|strong="H4993"\w*, \w Eliphelehu|strong="H466"\w*, \w Mikneiah|strong="H4737"\w*, \w Obed-edom|strong="H5654"\w*, \w Jeiel|strong="H3273"\w*, \w and Azaziah|strong="H5812"\w* \w were to lead the music|strong="H5329"\w* \w with lyres|strong="H3658"\w* \w according to|strong="H5921"\w* \w Sheminith|strong="H8067"\w*.\f + \fr 15:21 \fqa Sheminith\ft is probably a musical term; here and in \ref Psalm 6:1|PSA 6:1\ref* and Psalm 12:1.\f* \v 22 \w Chenaniah|strong="H3663"\w* \w the head|strong="H8269"\w* \w Levite|strong="H3881"\w* \w was the director|strong="H3256"\w* \w of the music|strong="H4853"\w* \w because|strong="H3588"\w* \w he was|strong="H1931"\w* \w highly skilled|strong="H995"\w*.
